<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Korea and Japan</p><h1 class="st-title">Date clan domain</h1><p class="st-meta">1542 CE – 1600 CE (approx.) · capital Yonezawa, later Iwadeyama</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The domain of the Date of southern Mutsu, which under the one-eyed Date Masamune briefly dominated northeastern Japan.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Date had long held lands in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutsu-province">Mutsu</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/date-tanemune">Date Tanemune</a> issued the detailed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jinkaishu">Jinkai-shu</a> law code in 1536, and from 1542 a war with his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/date-harumune">Harumune</a> split the clan; Harumune won and in 1548 moved the family seat to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yonezawa">Yonezawa</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Date built power through marriage alliances with neighbouring families across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tohoku-region">Tohoku</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/date-masamune">Date Masamune</a>, who lost an eye to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">smallpox</a> as a child, became head in 1584 and expanded aggressively, defeating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashina-clan">Ashina</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-suriagehara">Suriagehara</a> in 1589 to take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aizu">Aizu</a>, briefly controlling much of southern Tohoku.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/date-masamune">Masamune</a> submitted late to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> in 1590, lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aizu">Aizu</a> and in 1591 was moved to Iwadeyama. Siding with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> in 1600, he founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sendai-domain">Sendai Domain</a>, which the Date ruled until 1871.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/date-clan-domain.jpg" alt="Date clan domain" width="320" height="270"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Take_ni_Suzume.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1542 CE – 1600 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Yonezawa, later Iwadeyama</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Date Tanemune, Date Harumune, Date Masamune</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Japanese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/japan">Japan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Date clan, Date of Mutsu</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1571&amp;focus=date-clan-domain" aria-label="Date clan domain on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8173 814 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Date clan domain lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8493 1070L8440 1178M8493 1070L8505 1059"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8440 1178h0M8505 1059h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8493 1070h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8493 1070h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Yonezawa. <a href="/atlas?year=1571&amp;focus=date-clan-domain">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
